  "description": "Read PyPI download statistics from a workflow. Get a package's downloads over the last day, week and month, or its full daily series over the 180 days PyPI Stats keeps, with the total, the average per day, the busiest day and how the window compares with the one before it. Split those downloads by Python major version, by minor version to see whether 3.9 can be dropped, or by operating system to see which wheels are worth building. Compare several packages side by side, ranked with each one's share. Mirror traffic is excluded by default, so the figures are real installs. Every action reads: nothing here changes anything. No account or API key required.",
  "display_name": "PyPI Stats",
  "id": "pypi_stats"
}
